  "id": "DrugBank_DB00146 - MONDO_5520",
  "verbalization": "Calcifediol is implicated in the pathogenesis of rickets through a series of interconnected biological pathways. The evidence suggests that Calcifediol is linked to osteomalacia, a condition characterized by impaired bone mineralization, and this condition is further associated with dihydrotachysterol or cholecalciferol. These intermediates are known to play a role in calcium homeostasis and bone development, which are critical for rickets. The presence of multiple indirect pathways—each linking Calcifediol to rickets via different intermediates—supports a mechanism where Calcifediol influences phosphorus metabolism and calcium regulation, ultimately contributing to the development of rickets. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential role for Calcifediol in the regulation of bone health, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
